---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LessonIllustration from "../../components/LessonIllustration.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Maps"
  description="Compare ways to store named values when people edit them at the same time."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="Maps"
>
  <article class="map-family">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structure family</p>
      <h1>Maps</h1>
      <p>
        The ranger turns the Eagle Creek reports into a field record with named
        fields. Alice, Bob, and Carol now need rules for different answers,
        removed entries, and folders that can disappear and return.
      </p>
      <LessonIllustration id="structures-maps" />
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="shared-map-title">
      <header><div><p class="structure-kind">Uses shared order</p><h2 id="shared-map-title">SharedMap</h2><p>One shared order chooses a value for each name.</p></div><code>map_kernel</code></header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Alice writes <code>gate-status = Trail open</code>. Bob writes
            <code>Trail closed</code> before he sees her update. The ranger's
            service places Bob's change last, so every map keeps Bob's value.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul><li>Shared JSON settings managed by one service</li><li>Named values where the service can choose the last change</li></ul>
        </div>
        <dl><div><dt>Values</dt><dd>JSON and supported handles</dd></div><div><dt>When answers differ</dt><dd>Keep the last numbered change for each name</dd></div><div><dt>Removal</dt><dd>Delete one value or clear the map</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/shared-map/">Open the SharedMap lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="lww-map-title">
      <header><div><p class="structure-kind">No shared order</p><h2 id="lww-map-title">LWWMap</h2><p>The time on each change chooses the value.</p></div><code>lww_map_kernel</code></header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            The newest time can choose a different value than the service's
            delivery order. For each name, the map remembers the winning value
            or removal, along with its time and author.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul><li>Offline text settings that need one predictable winner</li><li>Maps where clocks, not delivery order, define "last"</li></ul>
        </div>
        <dl><div><dt>Values</dt><dd>Text</dd></div><div><dt>When answers differ</dt><dd>Later time, removal, then author</dd></div><div><dt>Removal</dt><dd>Remember the removal and its time</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/lww-map/">Open the LWWMap lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="or-map-title">
      <header><div><p class="structure-kind">No shared order</p><h2 id="or-map-title">OR-map</h2><p>New work can survive a removal made at the same time.</p></div><code>or_map_kernel</code></header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Alice removes the Eagle Creek stockpile after observing 5 crates.
            Bob records 3 more before he sees her removal. Alice's removal
            cannot erase work she has not seen, so the stockpile remains with
            all 8 crates.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul><li>Named ledgers and values that combine their own changes</li><li>Maps where new work must survive a removal made at the same time</li></ul>
        </div>
        <dl><div><dt>Values</dt><dd>Counts, shared fields, or text sets</dd></div><div><dt>When answers differ</dt><dd>New unseen work stays</dd></div><div><dt>Removal</dt><dd>Remove only the versions already seen</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/or-map/">Open the OR-map lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="directory-title">
      <header><div><p class="structure-kind">Uses shared order</p><h2 id="directory-title">SharedDirectory</h2><p>A folder tree that knows when a folder is replaced.</p></div><code>directory_kernel</code></header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Alice and Bob both create an Eagle Creek folder. The directory
            combines both creations into one path. It also keeps old edits from
            attaching to a new folder that later uses the same name.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul><li>Shared project and document folders</li><li>Folder trees where names can be reused</li></ul>
        </div>
        <dl><div><dt>Values</dt><dd>Folders and named entries</dd></div><div><dt>When answers differ</dt><dd>Use shared order and track each folder separately</dd></div><div><dt>Removal</dt><dd>Delete one specific folder</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/shared-directory/">Open the SharedDirectory lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section class="family-comparison" aria-labelledby="map-choice-title">
      <h2 id="map-choice-title">Choose what happens when answers differ</h2>
      <table aria-label="Map comparison">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Need</th><th scope="col">Choose</th><th scope="col">Main cost</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">One service orders JSON changes</th><td>SharedMap</td><td>The service must stay available</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Clocks choose text values</th><td>LWWMap</td><td>Remember clocks and removals</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">New work survives removal</th><td>OR-map</td><td>Remember which work each person saw</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Folders can reuse names</th><td>SharedDirectory</td><td>Track each folder separately</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through structures">
      <a href="/structures/registers/">Back to registers</a>
      <a href="/structures/shared-map/">Start the map lessons</a>
      <a href="/structures/">Return to structures</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .map-family { max-width: var(--measure-reading); margin-inline: auto; }
  .page-intro { margin-bottom: var(--space-7); }
  .page-intro > p:last-of-type { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .map-family > section:not(.family-comparison) {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    background: var(--clear);
  }
  section > header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }
  section h2, section header p { margin: 0; }
  section h2 { margin-block: var(--space-1); }
  .structure-kind { color: var(--instrument); font: 700 0.75rem/1 var(--font-data); }
  section header code { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  .structure-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(15rem, 0.7fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
  }
  .structure-body :is(p, h3) { margin-top: 0; }
  .structure-body h3 { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); font-size: 1rem; }
  dl { margin: 0; border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line); }
  dl div { padding-block: var(--space-3); }
  dl div + div { border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line-faint); }
  dt { color: var(--muted); font: 700 0.8rem/1.3 var(--font-ui); }
  dd { margin: var(--space-1) 0 0; }
  .structure-link { font-family: var(--font-ui); font-weight: 700; }
  .family-comparison { margin-top: var(--space-7); }
  table { width: 100%; margin-block: var(--space-4); border-collapse: collapse; }
  :is(th, td) { padding: var(--space-3); border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { font-family: var(--font-ui); }
  .structure-next {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
    border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  @media (width < 48rem) {
    section > header, .structure-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    section > header { display: grid; }
  }
</style>
